#: src/command-line-options.md:1
msgid "Command-line Options"
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:3
msgid ""
"`just` supports a number of useful command-line options for listing, "
"dumping, and debugging recipes and variables:"
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:6
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just --list\n"
"Available recipes:\n"
"  js\n"
"  perl\n"
"  polyglot\n"
"  python\n"
"  ruby\n"
"$ just --show perl\n"
"perl:\n"
"  #!/usr/bin/env perl\n"
"  print \"Larry Wall says Hi!\\n\";\n"
"$ just --show polyglot\n"
"polyglot: python js perl sh ruby\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:22
msgid "Setting Command-line Options with Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:24
msgid "Some command-line options can be set with environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:26
msgid ""
"For example, unstable features can be enabled either with the `--unstable` "
"flag:"
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:33
msgid "Or by setting the `JUST_UNSTABLE` environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:40
msgid ""
"Since environment variables are inherited by child processes, command-line "
"options set with environment variables are inherited by recursive "
"invocations of `just`, whereas command-line options set with arguments are "
"not."
msgstr ""

#: src/command-line-options.md:44
msgid ""
"Consult `just --help` for which options can be set with environment "
"variables."
msgstr ""
